      "title": "Letterboxd review of Oblivion",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Oblivion\"] I love sci-fi westerns so much (space westerns?) and I reaaaaaallly wanted to love this one more. I did enjoy the stop motion scorpions, the wacky town of Oblivion, and the frog arm wrestling scene. Most of all, Musetta Vander as Lash was sooooooo hot and badass with her assless chaps, latex gloves and whip!!!! The rest of the cast was surprisingly great too…featuring Julie Newmar, Issac Hayes, and George Takei as a screaming drunk doctor for some reason. Will still watch the sequel for more Lash though <3",
      "link": "https://letterboxd.com/film/oblivion/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Letterboxd review of Oblivion",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Oblivion\"] It's called Oblivion, but lose the image that just popped into your head because this movie is much closer to Fallout... New Vegas... with far too many mods installed. Heck, the main bad guy is basically a super mutant, and radscorpions roam the wastes.However, just like the aforementioned Bethesda game, it barely works with all those add-ons you downloaded. Sam Irvin, it's time to uninstall and try again.",
