      "title": "Letterboxd review of Oblivion",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Oblivion\"] The only real problem this has for me is pacing. It's fun enough, the cast is STACKED (Double Divoff, Julie Newmar, Struycken, Meg Foster, Musetta Vander who I only know as Sindel from MK Annihilation) and there's some dope animation sprinkled throughout; but it feels so much like a TV pilot in its leisurely approach to conflict. Definite potential for an even better sequel, tho.",
      "link": "https://letterboxd.com/film/oblivion/"
